# Build context is the repo root (see railway.json / render.yaml).
# Keep the context small and never send secrets or host artifacts.
#
# This file has to live at the root, not next to a Dockerfile: Docker reads
# `.dockerignore` from the *context* directory, so one sitting in `apps/api/` is
# silently never read — which is how a 700MB node_modules tree ends up being
# uploaded to the daemon on every build.
#
# It is shared by BOTH images — apps/api/Dockerfile and apps/web/Dockerfile —
# since both build from this context. Anything excluded here is excluded from
# both, which is why `apps/web` is not excluded even though the API image has no
# use for it: doing so would leave the web build with no source to compile. See
# apps/api/Dockerfile.dockerignore for how the API build drops it anyway.
#
# The `**/` prefixes matter: a bare `node_modules` matches only the one at the
# root, leaving every workspace's copy in the context.

.git
.github
.claude
.gitignore
.dockerignore

**/node_modules
**/dist
**/dist-seed
**/build
**/coverage
**/.turbo
**/.cache
**/*.tsbuildinfo

.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Docs and local tooling — not required at runtime.
*.md
!apps/api/**/*.md
docker-compose.yml
render.yaml
railway.json
vercel.json
apps/web/vercel.json

# Tests and editor noise
**/*.test.ts
**/*.spec.ts
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
**/*.log
**/npm-debug.log*
**/.vscode
**/.idea
